[agent] Done. The training dataset `churntraining30fee3`, version 1, exists on the platform and is verified.
[agent] **What was built** (project `mlpabaa1fcd`):
[agent] - Five feature groups: `transactions30fee3` (loaded from both the base and the late export), `profiles30fee3`, `activity30fee3`, `health30fee3` — each with `account_id` as primary key and `event_time` as the event-time column — plus `labels30fee3` with `label_time` as its event-time column.
[agent] - Feature view **`churntraining30fee3` v1**: labels as the base, LEFT-joined on `account_id` to each feature group selecting only the needed columns, so Hopsworks performs the point-in-time (as-of) join against `label_time`.
[agent] - **Training dataset version 1**, materialized as parquet via the Hopsworks Feature Query Service.
[agent] **Verification (all run as platform jobs, since that's where compute lives):** reading the training dataset back through the feature-view API returns exactly `account_id, label_time, amount, balance, credit_score, tier, sessions_7d, health_score` plus the label `churned` — 100 rows, one per labels.csv row, no nulls. A platform-side cross-check recomputed the backward as-of join from the raw CSVs (including the late transactions) and compared every value: **0 mismatches across all 100 rows**.
[agent] Two environment notes worth reporting:
[agent] - Direct data-plane connections (HopsFS on port 8020, ArrowFlight on 5005) are unreachable from this sandbox, so client-side `fg insert` / `td read` fail locally; all ingestion and reads were routed through platform jobs over REST, which is the intended platform path anyway.
[agent] - The cluster's Query Service has a reproducible server-side bug when reading a raw HopsFS path (`FlightServerError: Set changed size during iteration`), which breaks the default `get_training_data` read even in-cluster. The REST fallback (`read_options={"use_spark": True}`) works correctly, and the materialized parquet itself is intact — this is a Query Service defect, not a data problem.
